#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# heaviside_lambda

#% text
# `heaviside_lambda(x)` gives the triangle function `1 - |x|` for |x| < 1 and 0 otherwise.

#% text
# `heaviside_lambda(x, y, ...)` gives the product of the triangles.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The derivative is `heaviside_theta(x + 1) - 2 heaviside_theta(x) + heaviside_theta(x - 1)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
heaviside_lambda(1/4)
#% output
#= 3/4

#% cell
heaviside_lambda([-3, -1, 0, 1/3, 1])
#% output
#= [0, 0, 1, 2/3, 0]

#% cell
heaviside_lambda(1/2, 1/4)
#% output
#= 3/8

#% cell
d(heaviside_lambda(x), [x, 2])
#% output
#= dirac_delta(-1 + x) + dirac_delta(1 + x) - 2*dirac_delta(x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `heaviside_pi`, `heaviside_theta`, `unit_triangle`, `triangle_wave`
